# s7_keygen_tight: the dealer constructor's three pinned host buffers sized to measured need
# (patches/patch_keygen_tight.py).
#
# impl_lever: patches/patch_keygen_tight.py
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: SIGMAKeygen
# not_selectable_until: s6_dealer_window
# cost_class: free
# evidence: exact
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pool       W_host 9.17, W_vram 2.92 at s6 (steps.csv).
# object     s6 host peak = non-leader's (2,149,836 kB raw, 2,140,420 kB after recorder table);
#            rank 1 (steps/s6_dealer_window/peak-objects.md, job 47048628):
#            heap:SIGMAKeygen<unsigned long>::SIGMAKeygen(...) <- gpu_mem.cu:77:cpuMalloc, 1,179,660 kB,
#            0.5508 of attributed. Three allocations (backend/sigma.h, s6 tree):
#              sigma.h:371  keyBuf = cpuMalloc(keyBufSize)        1,073,745,920 B   the s6 key window, 1 GiB
#              sigma.h:392  llamaBuf1 = cpuMalloc(64 MiB)            67,112,960 B   LLAMA layernorm keys, own party
#              sigma.h:393  dummyBuf1 = cpuMalloc(64 MiB)            67,112,960 B   LLAMA layernorm keys, other party
#            cpuMalloc = posix_memalign + cudaHostRegister (pinned, resident at full size); one anon
#            mapping of 1,207,971,840 B (objects_resident_3418849.jsonl).
# timing     non-leader trace (poll_3418849/vmrss.log): 2,138,896 kB at 1.2 s, 2,149,828 kB at 7.8 s
#            (dealer phase, window live); 1,236,504 kB at 9.0 s (close() frees the window). Online
#            maxima: 1,968,900 kB polled (non-leader), 2,075,212 kB polled (leader; VmHWM 2,142,220
#            set in its dealer phase). llamaBuf/dummyBuf stay resident in the online phase (67.1 MB rows).
# need       largest operation 825,125,000 B (SNNI_KW|op_high; p_keywindow_high and s6, both parties);
#            llamaBuf 281,856 B per round, dummyBuf 6,764,544 B total (SNNI_BUF, s4 onwards). Slack
#            248,616,824 + 66,827,008 + 60,344,320 B = 375.8 MB pinned, never written.
#              key window  1 GiB  -> 800 MiB  (838,860,800 B, 1.017x the largest operation)
#              llamaBuf   64 MiB  ->   1 MiB  (3.7x)
#              dummyBuf   64 MiB  ->   8 MiB  (1.24x)
# checks     kwNote() asserts the window after every appending operation (new; s6's close() assert
#            bounded only the tail); every layernorm round asserts both LLAMA buffers; build refuses a
#            binary missing any of the three strings.
# kind       over-allocation (as s2..s5); open arm, own mechanism (s5_keybuf_tight) on s6's buffer.
# order      s6 paid; window created by s6, group rank 1 only from s6 (s5 rank 1: heap:main <-
#            ...cpuMalloc, 17,956,876 kB): not_selectable_until.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cost       free (same kernels, bytes, order; smaller cudaHostRegister range); declared (n=1).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
